    "status": "present",
    "value": "For the latest m stream values, remove the k smallest and k largest occurrences and return the floor mean of the middle; return minus one before m values. The approach is: sliding window with count/sum Fenwick trees; rank-prefix sums remove both tails including duplicate boundaries. Its target cost is O(log U) per method/O(m+U) space, U=100000. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
